Scope
-----
This record covers Windows-host portability defects discovered by the complete
pre-push hook after the GitHub run-7 contract correction. It contains no
Provider credential, price, candle, AIS/cargo assertion or news-causality
claim. No main mutation, force push, merge or deployment occurred.

Pre-push attempt 1
------------------
Result: FAIL (retained, not reclassified)
Cause: railway-watch-path-audit compared repository-relative Windows paths
with POSIX route namespaces. Backslashes prevented server/runtime ownership
from being recognized even though the dependency graph itself was valid.

Correction: a6157e5d83caae0e85d68fc8a7fcde15d33f2915
- Normalize repository-relative paths with path.sep before namespace checks.
- Use path.basename for the dynamic server-root boundary.
- Targeted railway audit suite: 82/82 PASS, exit 0.
- Typecheck, lint and tracked-diff checks: PASS, exit 0.

Pre-push attempt 2
------------------
Result: FAIL (retained, not reclassified)
Changed-suite result: 2,899 tests; 2,890 pass; 6 fail; 3 skip.
Causes:
- Five deployment-gate fixture assertions passed Windows host paths directly
  into a Git-for-Windows Bash/Python fixture.
- One edge import-graph assertion used a platform-dependent suffix comparison.

Correction: 5c5ca912fd04b78e939f9032b5d22d63d125d556
- Convert only fixture paths crossing the Bash boundary to POSIX form.
- Resolve the Bash executable on the Windows host before constructing the
  fixture PATH.
- Supply a fixture-local python3 wrapper that forwards to the real Python
  executable instead of the Windows Store alias.
- Compare the edge import target with the exact platform-resolved path.
- Targeted deployment/edge suites: 9/9 PASS, exit 0.
- Typecheck, lint and tracked-diff checks: PASS, exit 0.

